# AURELIA FC — frontend environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and adjust for your environment:
#     Copy-Item .env.example .env        # PowerShell
#     cp .env.example .env               # bash
#
# `.env` and `.env.local` are git-ignored. Only variables prefixed with `VITE_`
# are exposed to the browser bundle, so NEVER put secrets in this file.

# Absolute origin of the Aurelia FC API.
#
# Leave this EMPTY in development: the Vite dev server proxies `/api` requests to
# the backend (see the `server.proxy` block in vite.config.ts), so the browser
# talks to the same origin and no CORS pre-flight is needed.
#
# Set it to an absolute URL when the SPA is served from a different origin than
# the API (for example a production build hosted on a CDN or a separate host):
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.aurelia-fc.example.com
#
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
